## Critical Gotchas

- **No inline SQL** — every DB call goes through the project's data-access layer (see `.ai/governance/coding-standards.md` for the exact mechanism).
- **DB schema & stored procedures are authoritative via the data dictionary (if present)** — before preparing
  any SQL script, doing data analysis, or changing code that touches the DB, consult
  [`.ai/data-dictionary/`](.ai/data-dictionary/README.md) if it exists (`db-schema-dictionary.md` for every
  table/column/type/description, `stored-procedures.md` for every existing procedure's full
  script, `stored-procedure-dataflows.md` for a visual diagram of what each procedure touches).
  For non-SQL-Server projects this folder may not exist yet — see
  [`.ai/governance/SQL_Guidelines.md`](.ai/governance/SQL_Guidelines.md) for the current engine's data-dictionary
  status; where it is absent, fall back to `.ai/knowledge-base.md` Section 7 and ask the user.
  Never invent a table, column, or stored procedure name — verify against the data dictionary
  (when present) or the knowledge base first, same priority tier as `.ai/knowledge-base.md`.
- **No raw markup in templates/views** — use the project's own component/helper conventions (see `.ai/governance/coding-standards.md`).
- **No hardcoded strings** — all user-facing labels/text come from the project's resource/localization mechanism (see `.ai/governance/coding-standards.md`).
- **CSS theme files** — Module-specific pages touch the following theme folders: {{THEME_FOLDERS}}; shared pages touch at minimum the base theme folder and the accessibility theme folder from that set. See [coding-standards.md](.ai/governance/coding-standards.md#3-css--theme-rules) for paths.
- **Never push without explicit "PUSH" approval** from the user.
- **Shared library changes** (`{{SHARED_LIBS}}`) require team lead sign-off before implementation.
- **Branch must be `{{BASE_BRANCHES}}`** before starting any Bug / Enhancement / Change Request work.
- **NEVER post notes or comments to a ticket in the ticket tracker** under any circumstances, for any ticket type, at any workflow step. This is an absolute prohibition — no automatic, implicit, or proactive ticket comments. The only exception is when the user explicitly says "add note in ticket" and provides the note text.
- **Base classes** — follow the project's base-class conventions for view models/controllers/handlers (see `.github/skills/patterns/SKILL.md`).

